                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "For an Early Access game, Moribund is at a complete state regarding its core gameplay mode. The content provided is more than enough to have fun with your friends, especially regarding the available levels. Moreover, I didn't encounter any bugs affecting the experience.\n\nRegarding gameplay, you may need 10 minutes to get a good grasp of the game. After a few matches the whole concept of immobilize, then execute the other players, becomes quite clear and shows its potential. You can come up with a lot of strategies as to how to eliminate the other players. Trying to escape by pressing continuously the A button is really rewarding when accomplished, but also infuriating if you are the executioner, which helps build a competitive atmosphere with your friends, and scream eventually in their faces. One of the most well done aspects of the game, is the level design. You can ambush or escape using multiple routes, while the traps are well thought out and add to the gameplay.\n\nIt would be nice if the character's visual appearance popped out more. Some of the voice overs may need more work. I would like to see in the future team battles, more levels and traps.\n\nGenerally me and my friends found the game quite fun and kept playing for more than a few hours. Fans of the genre should give it a try.",
